  "feature": "Private versioned vehicle/driver documents and payload checks before departure",
  "database": "transportseva",
  "status": "Implemented and locally verified",
  "behavior": [
    "Providers submit RC, motor insurance, fitness, permit/authorisation and PUC evidence; driver licence evidence is separate.",
    "Authorized KYC staff document approval or rejection; revocation and renewals preserve earlier versions and files.",
    "Reviewed permitted payload must fit RC gross minus unladen weight and the registered declaration; client capacity fields do not override it.",
    "Missing, pending, rejected, revoked, expired, unavailable or mismatched evidence and overload block future Start Trip.",
    "Dates are inclusive in India and evaluated on today or a later pickup date. Permit/PUC applicability exceptions require documented staff decisions.",
    "Provider route/asset/load attestation is required; successful departure freezes the exact evidence versions and payload/load figures.",
    "Subcontracted and legacy unmapped vehicles use private booking-specific evidence. Legacy driver linking requires matching owned identity.",
    "Admin review bells navigate to the exact evidence; provider decision bells navigate to the asset and affected booking status notices to the exact booking.",
    "Shippers can read dispatch readiness and departure snapshots but cannot download the private documents.",
    "Historical departures have no invented retrospective approval; later renewals cannot rewrite their snapshots."
  ],
  "boundaries": {
    "review_method": "Documented manual review; not government database verification or automatic route-authorisation certification",
    "test_documents": "Synthetic QA PNGs, explicitly labelled; do not use these records as genuine compliance evidence.",
